KMBR Expo — Quick Start Checklist
=================================

BEFORE ANYTHING:
[ ] Read INITIAL_SETUP_SUMMARY.md (2 min)
[ ] Read README.md (3 min)

INSTALLATION:
[ ] npm install (5-10 min depending on connection)

VERIFY SETUP:
[ ] npm run type-check (should pass with no errors)
[ ] npm test (should see "PASS  src/domain/use-cases/__tests__/example.test.ts")
[ ] npm run lint (should pass with no errors)

START DEVELOPMENT:
[ ] npm run dev (should open Expo dev server on localhost:19000)
[ ] Scan QR code with phone or open web preview
[ ] See "Bem-vindo ao KMBR" on screen

OPTIONAL - Setup E2E Testing:
[ ] npm run prebuild (generates android/ and ios/)
[ ] npm run detox:build:ios (or detox:build:android)
[ ] npm run detox:test:ios (or detox:test:android)

CREATING YOUR FIRST FEATURE:
[ ] Read DEVELOPMENT.md (understand architecture)
[ ] Create PRD: /create-prd "Feature Name"
[ ] Create User Stories: /create-user-stories "Feature Name"
[ ] Implement following domain-first pattern
[ ] Write tests

FILES TO READ FIRST:
1. INITIAL_SETUP_SUMMARY.md — This setup guide
2. README.md — Project overview
3. DEVELOPMENT.md — How to build features
4. CLAUDE.md — Project conventions
5. e2e/README.md — Testing guide (when needed)

USEFUL COMMANDS:
npm run dev                    Start web development
npm run ios                    Start iOS simulator
npm run android                Start Android emulator
npm run type-check            Check TypeScript
npm run lint                  Lint code
npm run format                Format with Prettier
npm test                      Run unit tests
npm run detox:build:ios       Build E2E (iOS)
npm run detox:test:ios        Run E2E (iOS)

PROJECT STRUCTURE:
src/domain/                    Business logic (no dependencies)
src/adapters/                  Concrete implementations
src/infrastructure/            Setup & DI container
src/ui/                        React Native components & screens
e2e/                          End-to-end tests (Detox + Cucumber)

NEXT IMMEDIATE STEPS:
1. npm install
2. npm run dev
3. Verify you see the welcome screen
4. Read DEVELOPMENT.md
5. Create your first PRD with /create-prd

═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
IMPORTANT RULES:
═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
✓ Never call AsyncStorage/SQLite/SecureStore directly from components
✓ Domain must NOT import from adapters, infrastructure or ui
✓ Always use testID for selectable elements in E2E tests
✓ TypeScript strict: true (never use 'any')
✓ Use Zod to validate external data
✓ No data leaves the device (local-only storage)
✓ Siga DDD pattern: Domain → Adapter → Hook → Component

═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
ARCHITECTURE DIAGRAM:
═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
       UI Components & Screens
              ↓
         Custom Hooks
              ↓
        Zustand Stores
              ↓
       Dependency Container
              ↓
         Adapters (SQL, Storage)
              ↓
         Domain (Pure Logic)
              ↓
        No outgoing dependencies

═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

Status: ✅ READY TO CODE

Run this first: npm install && npm run dev
